CORE
write.c
--isr isr
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 10 the handler may run around the write: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 11 the handler need not run: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
--isr isr makes isr an interrupt handler, which may run before each access that
conflicts with the handler's reads and writes, and after each such write. The
calls are optional, hence both assertions fail.
